  _category: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 67eb6452bf5f2224083042268f30f622, type: 2}
  _glyph: "\U0001F9F0\uFE0F"
  _subtitle: Where are the scripts to access Lore data at runtime?
  _description: 'The Runtime API comes with the package (Packages/Lore/Runtime);
    there is nothing to copy. Give a MonoBehaviour a field of type LoreProject or
    Entry, assign the asset, and read values, e.g. entry.GetInt("Health").


    Examples:
    the Scripts folder of this demo (OzJourney.cs has the game rules, Generated/OzFields.cs
    the generated Field constants) and the Runtime API sample (Package Manager >
    Lore > Samples). The full reference is Documentation~/RuntimeAPI.md in the package.'
